+      <a href="security.html">Security guide</a>
+      <a href="threat-modeling.html">Threat modeling</a>
+      <a href="modules.html">Module reference</a>
+    </nav>
+    <p class="sidebar-note">Each tutorial is copied from a retained run through both front doors, own host and Knox. The outputs are what Aegis actually answered, not illustrations.</p>
+  </aside>
+  <main>
+    <header id="start" class="hero">
+      <p class="eyebrow">TUTORIALS</p>
+      <h1>Run real Apache software, with an agent governed by Aegis.</h1>
+      <p class="lead">Every tutorial puts Aegis between an IDE agent and one piece of real Apache software on a single machine. Start with the Hello World guide for the shape of the setup, then pick a deep-dive walkthrough or the project you already operate. New reviewers should read the security guide first.</p>
+      <div class="actions">
+        <a class="button primary" href="hello-world.html">Start Hello World</a>
+        <a class="button" href="../TUTORIALS.html">Rendered tutorial index</a>
+        <a class="button" href="security.html">Security guide</a>
+      </div>
+    </header>
+
+    <section id="deep">
+      <p class="eyebrow">DEEP DIVES</p>
+      <h2>Complete walkthroughs, step by step.</h2>
+      <p>These carry the full developer path: a tiny dataset or workload, an IDE agent, a governed change, and the same run through both front doors where noted.</p>
+      <div class="cards">
+        <article><h3><a href="../TUTORIAL-SPARK-ICEBERG.html">Spark and Iceberg from your IDE</a></h3><p>Spark 4.0.1 over Spark Connect with Iceberg 1.10.1 tables on a REST catalog. Own host and Knox 3.0.0, with VS Code, Kiro, Cursor, Claude Desktop and the MCP Python SDK. The complete developer path.</p></article>
+        <article><h3><a href="../TUTORIAL-SPARK-AND-SPARK-CONNECT.html">Spark and Spark Connect</a></h3><p>Spark 4.0.1 monitoring REST API and Spark Connect through a scripted client. Run Spark jobs and SQL through an agent.</p></article>
+        <article><h3><a href="../TUTORIAL-ICEBERG.html">Iceberg REST catalog</a></h3><p>The Iceberg 1.10.1 RESTCatalogServer with resource scopes, approvals and destructive-operation receipts over namespaces, properties and drops.</p></article>
+        <article><h3><a href="../TUTORIAL-KAFKA-AND-KAFKA-CONNECT.html">Kafka and Kafka Connect</a></h3><p>A Kafka 3.9.1 KRaft broker and a Connect worker. Govern topic administration and the connector lifecycle.</p></article>
+        <article><h3><a href="../TUTORIAL-FLINK.html">Apache Flink</a></h3><p>Flink 1.20.1 jobs, jars, savepoints, stopping and cancellation, each as a governed action.</p></article>
+        <article><h3><a href="https://github.com/vaquarkhan/aegis-mcp-gateway/blob/main/examples/break-glass-mcp-servers/README.md">Break-glass MCP servers</a></h3><p>Spark, Kafka, Iceberg and Flink as one independent server each, with a signed server catalog and incident containment end to end. Repository walkthrough.</p></article>
+      </div>
+      <p class="callout">Evidence boundary: tutorials describe retained historical runs. Read the <a href="../VALIDATION.html">validation report</a> and <a href="../evidence/CLAIMS-MATRIX.html">claims matrix</a> before treating any integration as release-candidate evidence.</p>
+    </section>
+
+    <section id="projects" class="band">
+      <p class="eyebrow">ONE PER PROJECT</p>
+      <h2>An IDE-ready tutorial for each verified project.</h2>
+      <p>These are built by <code>tools/build-project-tutorials.py</code> from each project's retained run. All have historical own-host and Knox records, and every kept audit journal verifies. Each tutorial gives the engine command line, both front doors step by step, VS Code, Kiro and Cursor files, prompts mapped to tools with what Aegis answered, and the full request table of that run.</p>
+      <div class="table-wrap">
+        <table class="ref-table">
+          <thead><tr><th>Project</th><th>Version exercised</th><th>Tutorial</th></tr></thead>
+          <tbody>
+            <tr><td>Apache ActiveMQ</td><td>6.3.2 (Jolokia)</td><td><a href="../tutorials/activemq.html">Open tutorial</a></td></tr>
+            <tr><td>Apache Airflow</td><td>2.9.3</td><td><a href="../tutorials/airflow.html">Open tutorial</a></td></tr>
